<title>POLAND: Polish net reserves fall to $21.47 bln in Dec 1-10.</title>
<headline>Polish net reserves fall to $21.47 bln in Dec 1-10.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish net foreign currency reserves fell by $149 million in the December 1-10 period to $21.47 billion but were up $1.03 billion from the start of 1996, the National Bank of Poland said.</p>
<p> POLISH RESERVES (bln dollars)  DEC 1-10   NOV     OCT    DEC '95</p>
<p>  Net reserves			21.47     21.62   21.60    20.44</p>
<p>  Official reserves		 N/A	  N/A    17.70    14.96</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures in billions of dollars. Official reserves are those held by the state. Net reserves are the total amount of hard currencies in the whole banking system.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
